OL,3,AJournalist to be crowned king in Uganda
OL,4,Aafter bitter succession dispute
OL,5,
OL,6,FPrince Edward Rukidi Kijanangoma
OL,7,FNyabongo I, who is set to be crowned
OL,8,Fking of Uganda's Tooro kingdom later,
OL,9,Fhas long been a familiar face in the
OL,10,Fcountry.
OL,12,FFor many Ugandans, he was known not as
OL,13,Fthe heir to the throne, but as a
OL,14,Fstoryteller, as a long-serving anchor
OL,15,Fand editor at the state broadcaster.
OL,17,FBut Kijanangoma, 56, has now become the
OL,18,Fsubject of media attention himself -
OL,19,Fhis rise to the Tooro throne sparking
OL,20,Fcontroversy and widespread reactions
OL,21,Fbeyond the country.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
